module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.exact_duplicate_match_arm_not_refused

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data exact_duplicate_match_arm_not_refused: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "exact_duplicate_match_arm_not_refused" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an exact duplicate constructor pattern appears twice in one match, the second arm is unreachable, and the compiler accepts both -- so SOURCE ORDER silently decides which body answers** (INVALID STATE: two arms of one `match` name the SAME closed-variant constructor with DIFFERENT bodies. ",

    "HARM: the second body is dead, and nothing says so. ",

    "The author wrote it believing it would run; the reader cannot tell which of the two the machine picks without knowing the arm-selection rule; and the wrong one being first is a wrong answer that type-checks, projects and passes every gate. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN IS MINE AND IS MEASURED (gunbc#9981, 2026-09-03). ",

    "`probe_owner_is_wet_lib_module` in `v2.test.claim.self_host.stage0_executable_assembly_test` carried `WetActuatorLibModuleOwner` twice -- once as the matching arm binding `module_basename` and `declaration_route`, and again in the trailing list of `=> false` arms, where I had added it while enumerating the coproduct for exhaustiveness. ",

    "The compiler accepted it in every lane it reached. ",

    "It was found by a review reading the arm list, not by any check. ",

    "THIS IS THE DUAL OF EXHAUSTIVENESS, NOT AN INSTANCE OF IT. ",

    "Exhaustiveness asks whether the UNION of the arms covers the domain, and gunbc does refuse when it does not -- the same file's missing `WetActuatorLibModuleOwner` arm refused loudly earlier in the same PR. ",

    "The unasked question is whether each arm CONTRIBUTES an inhabitant no earlier arm already covers. ",

    "A duplicate arm makes the union no larger, so an exhaustiveness check is green by construction on exactly the source that carries this defect: adding the duplicate is the one edit that cannot move that verdict. ",

    "THE MEASURED GRAIN IS NARROW AND IS STATED NARROWLY, because the general form is not the same question. ",

    "Deciding whether an arbitrary later pattern is subsumed by the union of earlier ones is a coverage problem over guards, nested patterns and bindings; the measured specimen is the decidable corner of it -- two SYNTACTICALLY IDENTICAL closed-variant constructor heads at the same match. ",

    "Claiming the general form here would put a ratchet where a wall is available, and would let the narrow wall be cited as coverage for the broad class. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- the state is writable, accepted, and silent. ",

    "CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed, and the reason it is not 4 is that a `match` is written arm by arm, so a second identical head is spellable in any source a human or a generator can emit; no constructor arrangement removes it. ",

    "What rung 3 buys is that no `Accepted` program contains one. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: **a match-arm usefulness judgment in the compiler frontend that REFUSES a second arm whose constructor head is already covered, locating both the duplicate and the arm that covers it** -- with a discriminating RED (two identical constructor patterns, different bodies, refused at the second arm), an accepted positive control (two distinct constructor patterns, accepted), and a retention control establishing that adding a variant to the coproduct does not weaken the duplicate judgment. ",

    "A diagnostic that names the duplicate without refusing it does not discharge this: a warning on an accepted program is the tier DESIGN section 6 calls an inert lens, and this class is silent precisely because nothing stops the line.)",

    "**RECURRENCE, FOUR DAYS LATER, SAME AUTHOR, FOUND THE SAME WAY -- BY A REVIEWER READING THE ARM LIST** (gunbc#10723, review 61771, 2026-09-07). ",

    "`unrealized_actuator_steps_refuse_rather_than_reporting_absent` in `test.claim.nbd_proxy_virtual_media_install` carried `ActuatorStepRefused { cause: ActuatorStepActuatorHostUnsatisfiable }` TWICE in each of two of its three match blocks -- copy residue from pasting the new arm, at a different indentation from the arm it duplicated. ",

    "The witness ran GREEN with the duplicates present, which is the whole point: the recurrence is not evidence that the earlier filing was wrong, it is evidence that a filed class with a named trigger and no built wall keeps producing specimens. ",

    "WHAT THIS RECURRENCE ADDS IS THE ASYMMETRY MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS ON ONE FILE, rather than inferred across two incidents. ",

    "The row above states that exhaustiveness refuses a MISSING arm while saying nothing about a DUPLICATE one, citing the earlier specimen's other PR for the refusing half. ",

    "Here both halves were executed against the same tree minutes apart: deleting the arm refuses at resolve with `non-exhaustive match: missing variant(s) ActuatorStepRefused { cause: ActuatorStepActuatorHostUnsatisfiable }`, and duplicating it is accepted in silence. ",

    "One direction is a hard wall, the other is not looked at, and the compiler already walks the tree that would decide it. ",

    "A SECOND-ORDER RECEIPT FROM THE SAME REPAIR, worth carrying because the remedy nearly caused the defect it was removing: the fix was a `sed` keyed on the duplicates' column-4 indentation, and the FIRST block's legitimate arm sits at column 4 too, so the edit deleted three arms where two were duplicates. ",

    "That was caught by re-reading the region, and the control run afterwards would in fact have caught it as well -- the missing arm refuses -- which is the one direction this class does have a wall in. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, ADDED: an edit that removes a duplicated arm is keyed on the accident (whitespace, order, position) rather than on the identity, so it can only be verified by re-reading the arms it left behind, never by the green run that follows.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
